# Build context is the repo root for both images (infra/docker/*.Dockerfile). Keeping this
# tight matters more than usual: the `pruner` stage copies the whole context before turbo
# narrows it down, so anything listed here is never even sent to the daemon.

# Dependencies + build output — every stage installs and builds from the pruned lockfile,
# so host artifacts would only shadow them (and node_modules holds host-arch native builds
# of argon2, which must NOT leak into a linux/amd64 image).
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
storybook-static/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
.turbo/
coverage/
.pnpm-store/

# Secrets — apps/api/.env holds real JWT/encryption keys locally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS + tooling
.git/
.github/
.devcontainer/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Not needed to build or run either app.
# NOTE: `e2e/` is deliberately NOT excluded — pnpm-workspace.yaml declares it as a workspace,
# and removing it from the context risks a workspace-resolution failure in `turbo prune`.
# Likewise test/story sources stay: each package's own tsconfig already excludes them from
# its build, and dropping them from the context only risks a confusing tsc failure.
docs/
openspec/
debugging/
scripts/
.claude/
.claude-backup-*/
.superpowers/
infra/k8s/

# Logs / OS
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
